<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h2>CDEF Coverage Analysis</h2>
    <p class="text-body-secondary">
      Upload the Terraform this boundary is built from and SPARC will report which
      Component Definitions it needs: which to adopt from AWS Labs, which of your own
      to keep, which are still to be authored, and which you maintain but nothing deploys.
    </p>

    <%# #904 — the sensitivity note is on the screen, not only in the code. An
        operator is about to upload a file that may contain live credentials, and
        is entitled to know what happens to it before choosing the file. %>
    <div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
      <strong>Your state file is not stored.</strong>
      Terraform state can contain plaintext secrets — database passwords, private keys,
      account identifiers. SPARC reads only whether each resource is managed, its
      <em>type</em> (for example <code>aws_db_instance</code>), and how many there are.
      Resource attributes are never read, and the file itself is never saved. If you
      save the analysis, what is written is the list of services and counts, plus each
      file's name and SHA-256 checksum.
    </div>

    <%# `turbo: false` is load-bearing. Analyze renders its report with 200
        rather than redirecting, because the report is derived from the POSTed
        files and there is nothing to redirect TO — the upload is discarded, so
        a follow-up GET could not rebuild it. Turbo Drive refuses a non-redirect
        200 from a form ("Form responses must redirect to another location"),
        silently leaving the user on the upload screen. Only a browser catches
        that; request specs do not run Turbo. %>
    <%= form_with url: analyze_cdef_coverage_index_path, method: :post, multipart: true,
                  local: true, data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :authorization_boundary_id, @boundary&.id %>

      <%= render "shared/dropzone",
            form: f,
            field: :files,
            accept: ".json,.tfstate",
            multiple: true,
            hint: "Terraform state (.tfstate) or plan JSON (terraform show -json plan.tfplan). Upload every state that makes up the boundary — analysing one state of several reports the others' services as unused." %>

      <div class="d-flex gap-3 mt-3">
        <%= f.submit "Analyze coverage", class: "btn btn-success" %>
        <%= link_to "Cancel", (@boundary ? authorization_boundary_path(@boundary) : cdef_documents_path),
              class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h5">Saved analyses</h3>
    <p class="text-body-secondary mb-2">
      <%= link_to "View saved coverage runs", cdef_coverage_index_path %>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
